  m_Name: Caligo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ButterflyData
  speciesName: Caligo atreus
  description: "La Caligo atreus es una mariposa de la familia Nymphalidae, perteneciente
    al g\xE9nero Caligo.\r\n\r\nCaracter\xEDsticas principales:\r\n\r\nEs una especie
    nocturna y de gran tama\xF1o, alcanzando hasta 15 cm de envergadura.\r\nSu caracter\xEDstica
    m\xE1s distintiva son los ocelos en forma de ojos de b\xFAho en la parte inferior
    de sus alas, los cuales le permiten camuflarse y ahuyentar depredadores.\r\nLas
    larvas de esta mariposa se alimentan principalmente de plantas del g\xE9nero
    Heliconia (familia Heliconiaceae), que son herb\xE1ceas tropicales con inflorescencias
    coloridas y llamativas."
  speciesNameEn: 'Dark Mist '
  descriptionEn: 'The Caligo atreus is a butterfly of the Nymphalidae family , belonging
    to the genus Caligo .

    

    Main features:

    

    It is a large,
    nocturnal species, reaching up to 15 cm in wingspan .

    Its most distinctive
    feature is the owl-like eyespots on the underside of its wings, which allow it
    to camouflage itself and scare away predators.

    The larvae of this butterfly
    feed mainly on plants of the genus Heliconia (family Heliconiaceae), which are
    tropical herbaceous plants with colorful and showy inflorescences.'
